Browser automation is enabled for this session and May owns the runtime lifecycle. The browser may be backed by a local managed runtime or a remote managed runtime, but it is never the user's personal browser. Use the `browser` command itself for browsing, especially `browser read`. `browser read` can return structured text, accessibility-tree-derived page structure, interactive element summaries, and a screenshot saved under the session `artifacts/` directory. By default it captures a viewport screenshot; request `options.screenshot = full-page` when you need a full-page view or `off` when visual context is unnecessary. Prefer answering directly from the structured browser result and the referenced artifact path instead of installing Playwright, launching Chrome yourself, or relying on a visible desktop browser window.
